[1.410007, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.234718, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:ca215e551fa508db0a3cd8e50d604756852f98bd37a35276e58c4e42042f90c8\r\n  backup key: created and enrolled, private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/bc51df6284e03206abdaceb01ded0764caba8496d458b4d66c8334805f718e52.key\r\n"]
[2.234758, "o", "  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[2.235793, "o", "  Created AGENTS.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .claude/rules/mnema-instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .github/instructions/mnema-instructions.instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .cursor/rules/mnema-instructions.mdc, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[2.235887, "o", "  Each holds the mnema instructions an agent host reads at the start of a session: when to\r\n  call the mnema tools, and what never goes in the record. `mnema instructions --remove`\r\n  takes them out.\r\n\r\n  mnema writes no other file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n"]
[2.235906, "o", "  project in a file of its own (the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names), and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n"]
[2.235974, "o", "  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[2.236044, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n"]
[2.236062, "o", "  Off until switched on: edit-first-write-gate, user-corrections.\r\n  Turn one on with `mnema switch on <name>`; `mnema switch` lists every channel.\r\n"]
[2.236134, "o", "  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.845129, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
